<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Feb 1.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Feb 1.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Feb 1</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     265	   1.32     425400 112.73    25.97</p>
<p>State Bank	   270	   1.35     413150 111.55    26.07</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   182	   0.93     609400 110.91    26.64</p>
<p>ITC		    385	   1.93     165000  63.53    26.14</p>
<p>MTNL		   240	   1.20     256100  61.46    26.07</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    320	   1.63     157650  50.45    26.56</p>
<p>ACC		   1275	   5.90	23620  30.12    24.13</p>
<p>Tata Power	   132	   0.66     218900  28.89    26.07</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    235	   1.13     107150  25.18    25.07</p>
<p>BSES		   225	   1.10     101500  22.84    25.49</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 25.89 percent on an annualised basis against 24.99 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Jan 25.</p>
<p>The average badla charge takes into account the record date badla charges.The following scrips have gone into record date badla charges - Gujarat Ambuja Cements &amp; Ranbaxy Lab.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
